.TH "SET-WALLPAPER" "1" "November 2026" "arran4/dotfiles" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
set\-wallpaper \- show a Hyprland workspace\-specific wallpaper using swaybg
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBset\-wallpaper\fR
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Get the active Hyprland workspace ID. Select ~/Pictures/wallpapers/ID.jpg when present; otherwise use ~/Pictures/wallpapers/default.jpg. Start swaybg in the background using fill mode.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fB~/Pictures/wallpapers/ID.jpg\fR
Optional workspace\-specific wallpaper.
.TP
\fB~/Pictures/wallpapers/default.jpg\fR
Fallback wallpaper.
.SH NOTES
This script starts another swaybg process rather than managing the lifetime of earlier wallpaper processes.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
Requires Hyprland, hyprctl, swaybg, awk, cut and tr, plus
wallpaper JPG files in ~/Pictures/wallpapers.
.SH OPERATION
The current workspace ID selects ID.jpg; if it is not present,
default.jpg is used. swaybg is started in fill mode in the
background without stopping earlier swaybg instances.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
mkdir -p "$HOME/Pictures/wallpapers"
cp /path/to/image.jpg "$HOME/Pictures/wallpapers/default.jpg"
set-wallpaper
.fi
.SH TROUBLESHOOTING
Check active workspace ID and image paths if no wallpaper appears.
Repeated invocations can accumulate swaybg processes.
.SH SEE ALSO
hyprland\-keys(7)
